  "result": {
    "summary": "Verified the full commit diff (b4614aa) against the spec and all six acceptance tests plus the CLI test. Pinning logic (architecture/gotcha:open/decision:constraint/decision:security via the config-driven hot_never_compact list, plus ANY-open-source-task pinning using the queued/held/running allowlist resolved the same way as memory_store._goal_from_bus) is correct and matches every test scenario traced by hand. Candidate selection merges tier=warm and tier=hot from the new all_records() helper rather than only tier=warm; this is a deliberate and necessary deviation from the literal spec wording so that previously-hot records remain eligible candidates on the next build (required for the idempotency and byte-identical-second-run tests) \u2014 verified this is equivalent to 'every non-cold record' and does not violate 'cold unchanged'. Score/component-mention matching (whole-token, case-insensitive, scope basenames via Path.stem) matches spec, and the scope/write_scope fallback matches the established convention used identically in stale.py, jev_sched.py, speculation.py, skills_registry.py, jev_skills.py, evidence.py, and context_router.py. pool.toml hot_* keys sit under their own comment inside the existing [memory] table as required. cli.py wiring for 'memory hot [--json]' and 'memory compact' matches the spec, and rebuild() now emits the 'run memory compact' hint consistent with docs/hermes-hardening/07-hot-memory.md. Only issue found is the low-severity dead-code note above; nothing blocks approval.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
