        "issue": "The 'governing decision' pointer-line feature (spec: pointer line 'memory show <id>' only for dropped governing decisions) checks for tag 'governing' in record.get('tags', []), but nothing in memory_store.py (migrate's fixed tag_words list, or any other producer) ever sets a 'governing' tag on a decision record. dropped_decisions is therefore always empty in the current pipeline, making this branch effectively dead/unreachable and untested by any acceptance test. Not a regression and doesn't fail any listed acceptance criterion, but the spec requirement is not actually exercised.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
